**Read:** [Materials Processing — Chris Schuh, MIT 3.044](../sources/Materials-Processing-MIT-3-044.lingua#r_4V5BA7W1TFKGRTGNHN7ZTAK1TW), all mold, heat-transfer, solidification, and matching problem/exam work; [Material Processing: Metallurgical Aspects, Fundamental and Practical — Dwivedi](../sources/Material-Processing-Theory-and-Practice-NPTEL.lingua#r_7BSA0B8283WGYN6KF2609N2GK2), the entire casting and demonstration sequence; [Smitheries and Foundries Industry — European Commission BREF](../sources/Smitheries-and-Foundries-BREF.lingua#r_7ZJ5479WTSPDER11K364F6T041), whole relevant casting, mold/core, treatment, finishing, and utility chapters; [Aluminium Automotive Manual — European Aluminium and collaborators](../sources/Aluminium-Automotive-Manual.lingua#r_73MPKA19MDBSQ96195B818Z49T), the full applicable casting and product-quality material.

Casting joins melt preparation, transfer, mold/core behavior, filling, heat extraction, solidification, feeding, removal, and finishing. Geometry, surface/interfacial behavior, gases, inclusions, shrinkage, stress, and phase history affect the final product. The presence of a fully filled mold does not establish a qualified casting.

Derive a useful heat/flow or solidification-time relation with actual assumptions, material properties, contact/boundary conditions, and geometric scale. Empirical design correlations need their calibration range and definitions. A local thermal model alone cannot identify every entrainment, gas, feeding, chemical, or hot-tearing mechanism.

Compare metal, mold/core/binder, containment, atmosphere, cooling, tools, inspection, maintenance, and residual/recovery work on the whole accepted-product boundary. A higher gross casting yield or faster cycle may change defects, machining allowances, repair, or product performance.

**Work:** reconstruct two complete casting arrangements for a defined alloy/function. Independently reproduce a central heat/flow or material-balance result, verify numerical or empirical limits, and compare with measured temperature, structure, and defect observations. Investigate at least two plausible explanations for a defect, designing a discriminating test. Defend the preferred arrangement through quality, repeatability, uncertainty, utilities, tooling, residuals, and continuing maintenance.

**Continue:** [Reconstruct continuous casting through coupled flow, shell formation, chemistry, and work](Continuous-casting-flow-shell-growth-and-product-history.lingua#r_6SK54AG2Q53MB4RJPFS21GJ0VY).

